  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1159 AM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nSurface analysis reveals a strong 1038 mb high pressure system\ncentered over the Ohio River Valley, encompassing much of the\neastern CONUS, while a 1012 mb surface low is positioned over the\nGreat Basin. Upper-level analysis indicates an anomalous ridge\namplifying northward across the Plains, anchored between deep\ntroughing along the West Coast and a closed low near the Gulf\nCoast. Medium-range guidance maintains high confidence in the\nridge building across the Lower Mississippi and Ohio Valleys\nthrough late week, while the cut-off Gulf low tracks slowly\nnorthwestward toward the Tennessee Valley. Consequently, above-\nnormal temperatures are expected from Thursday into the weekend,\nwith 586 dam heights supporting afternoon highs reaching the\nlower to mid-70s.\n\nBy the weekend, the upper ridge weakens as synoptic flow\ntransitions to a southwesterly regime. Model guidance shows\nnotable divergence regarding upper-level evolution, though a\ngradual surge in atmospheric moisture is expected, evidenced by\nrising PWATs and low-level dewpoints across the mid-South. Rain\nchances remain limited throughout the extended period as LREF\nensemble guidance favors a split-flow regime.",
